WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.300
Thomas Aquinas held that the human soul
arrives some weeks after conception.

2
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.790
Today the Catholic Church
protects life from conception,

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.880
and teaches that direct abortion
is always gravely wrong.

4
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.430
Yet in a plural society, many
people reject that starting point.

5
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.050
Can ending a pregnancy ever be a
side-effect rather than a choice?

6
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.510
And what should the law do about it?

7
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.200
In this mission, you'll test natural law,

8
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:31.410
the theory that comes from
Aquinas, on real medical dilemmas.

9
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.790
Then you'll weigh up how far a nation's
laws should follow a moral theory that

10
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.970
many people don't share.

11
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.810
Your mission: find out whether ending
a pregnancy can ever be a side-effect,

12
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.360
and what the law should do.
